<BaseLayout
  title="Organizational record · America's School Trust Library"
  description="The Library's organizational record: what was filed, when, and by whom — registrations, incorporation, and the board actions that seated the founding board of America's School Trust Library."
  sourceId="organizing"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-a:text-blue-700 prose-a:underline">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Organizational record</h1>

    <p class="record-banner">
      <strong>Organizational record</strong> — This page is the Library's
      organizational record — what was filed, when, and by whom. The
      plan-version of this page, written before any of it had happened, was
      superseded August 3, 2026.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>
        This page once described, in the future tense, how the Library would
        become a legal organization. That work is done; the plan-version of
        this page is preserved in the Library's records, superseded August 3,
        2026. What follows is what actually happened.
      </em>
    </p>

    <h2>The record</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>July 10, 2026</strong> — Oregon Department of Justice Charitable
      Activities Registration No. 72571 acknowledged.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>July 15–16, 2026</strong> — Certificate of name compliance issued
      by the Division of Financial Regulation (corrected copy July 16),
      authorizing use of “Trust” in the corporate name.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>July 21, 2026</strong> — Articles of Incorporation e-filed with
      the Oregon Secretary of State. Oregon Registry No. 259005891.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>July 30, 2026</strong> — Federal Employer Identification Number
      issued (kept as an internal corporate record).
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>August 3, 2026</strong> — The founding board — David Sullivan,
      President; Barbara K. Sullivan, Treasurer; Kenneth Magee, Secretary —
      seated by unanimous written consent, adopting
      <a href="/bylaws/">Bylaws v7</a>, the
      <a href="/rights/">Constitution and Readers' Bill of Rights v1</a>, and a
      Conflict of Interest Policy v2. All published on the
      <a href="/governance/">governance page</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>August 9, 2026</strong> — The board added Barry Shane as a
      director and accepted the withdrawal of Barbara K. Sullivan. Offices were
      reassigned: David Sullivan, President and Treasurer; Kenneth Magee,
      Secretary. The board now has three directors; two seats remain open.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>August 10, 2026</strong> — The board of Oregon Advocates for
      School Trust Lands voted 3–0 to establish a non-exclusive strategic
      alliance with the Library, limited to information, education, and
      preservation, and carrying no control, no agency, no financial
      obligation, and no litigation position on either side. Either board may
      end it at any time. OASTL is the advocacy organization Dave Sullivan also
      serves as president; he disclosed the dual role and sat out the vote. The
      Library's board acted on the alliance on September 10, 2026; see the next
      entry.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>September 10, 2026</strong> — Unanimous written consent of the
      board, in seven resolutions, circulated by the President on September 7
      and signed in counterparts: Kenneth Magee by signed copy returned
      September 8; Barry Shane by written assent returned September 8; David
      Sullivan on September 10, the date the instrument took effect. On the two
      alliance resolutions David Sullivan disclosed his interest and took no
      part; Kenneth Magee and Barry Shane, each stating that he has no
      interest in either organization, approved them. The executed instrument
      and the Secretary's certificate are kept with the corporate records. What
      the board resolved:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Adopted as Version 1, September 2026, the six documents published at
        <a href="/participate/">Participate</a> — working editions, numbered
        and dated, which the board may revise at any time — and, for its own
        use and not published, a distribution plan.
      </li>
      <li>
        Accepted, on the Library's side, the alliance established by the
        August 10, 2026 resolution of Oregon Advocates for School Trust Lands:
        limited to information, education and preservation; not exclusive,
        controlling or financial; neither organization directing the other,
        owing the other money, or speaking for the other; the Library's
        <a href="/rights/">Constitution</a> governing if the two could ever
        be read to differ; either board free to end it. Approved by the two
        directors with no interest in that organization, Kenneth Magee and
        Barry Shane; David Sullivan, its president, disclosed his interest
        and took no part.
      </li>
      <li>
        Approved, on the Library's side and on the same terms, an alliance
        with Advocates for School Trust Lands, the national organization, on
        the terms of the resolution prepared for that board's meeting of
        August 13, 2026 — to take effect only if and when that board adopts
        it substantially in that form. The Library neither asks that board to
        adopt it nor sets it a date. As of September 10, 2026 that board has
        not acted. Approved by the same two directors; David Sullivan, a
        director of that organization, disclosed his interest and took no
        part.
      </li>
      <li>
        Directed the President to prepare and file the Library's application
        for federal tax-exempt recognition, on the full form, and to put the
        substantially complete application before the board before it is
        submitted; made the written finding the bylaws require for the
        President to hold the Treasurer's office as well, as a temporary and
        necessary arrangement that ends when a fourth director is seated or
        another Treasurer is elected, and no later than the election of
        officers in 2027; and adopted three amendments to the Articles of
        Incorporation &mdash; stating the Library's particular purposes,
        stating the order in which its assets would pass if the Library were
        ever wound up, and requiring two board votes thirty days apart to
        change those two articles &mdash; to be filed with the Oregon
        Secretary of State. Neither the application nor the amendments has
        yet been filed.
      </li>
      <li>
        Directed the Secretary to publish the postings for two director seats
        and the Law Librarian, with replies to the Secretary, Kenneth Magee,
        at library@schooltrusts.net. Published September 10, 2026 at
        <a href="/participate/open-seats/">Open seats</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Directed that the presidency be filled by a person other than the
        founder no later than December 31, 2027, with the search beginning
        now; recorded the founder's separation timetable, including that the
        Founders' Statement year ends about June 14, 2027, and asked the
        Secretary to bring the reconciliation to the board before March 31,
        2027.
      </li>
      <li>
        Ratified the correction of the Library's published description of
        its federal filing —
        <a href="/about/corrections/log/">corrections log entry 022</a>,
        September 8, 2026 — and confirmed that until a determination is in
        hand no Library page will describe the Library as exempt under the
        federal tax code, describe a contribution as tax-deductible, publish
        the Library's federal employer identification number, or carry a
        signature image.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      <strong>Open</strong> — the federal tax-exemption determination.
      America's School Trust Library is an Oregon nonprofit public benefit
      corporation. The Library has not yet filed its application for federal
      tax-exempt recognition; it is being prepared. No federal tax-exemption
      determination has been issued, and until one is, the Library does not
      describe contributions as tax-deductible. On September 10, 2026 the board
      directed that the application be prepared and put before it before
      submission.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Open</strong> — the alliance with Advocates for School Trust
      Lands, which takes effect on the Library's side only when that
      organization's board adopts its resolution; and the Articles of
      Amendment adopted by the board on September 10, 2026 and not yet filed.
    </p>
  </article>

